        <p>navy-blue velvet and white cloth appliques. The sleeves puff to the elbow, where they end in inverted gauntlet cuffs, trimmed to match the collar, the under-sleeves being of white cloth, laid in shallow pleats or folds. This costume should be completed with a white straw hat, bound and trimmed with blue velvet, after the manner of the one shewn in the sketch; or the same shape in navy- blue straw would look both smart and in keeping with the coat and skirt. GOSSIP.</p>
        <p>Mr. and Mrs. Henry Labouchere gave a fancy- dress ball at the Villa Christina, Florence, recently. Mrs. Labouchere appeared in a fancy costume as an English housekeeper, and Marchesa di Rudini (nit Labouchere) wore the costume of a Normandy peasant.</p>
        <p>Viscountess Hood, who has been staying in Rome, presented the Hon. Dorothy Hood to the Queen of Italy at the reception lately held at the Quirinal.</p>
        <p>A "Gibson Girl Protection Society" is in course of formation in New York. So many young women are affecting the airs and the walk of the artist's famous creation that the early clAimants to be the original Gibson girl have determined to assert their rights. In the early part of the season the Grand Duchess of Saxe-Coburg will pay another visit to England, bringing with her Princess Beatrice, who is very anxious to share with Princess Ena of Battenberg and the young Princesses of Connaught some of the gaieties of the London season.</p>
