      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1905-03-11_WidnesExaminer_art0114" n="art0114">
        <p>AWONDERFUL DISCOVRRY.—This is the age of research and experiment, when all nature, so to speak, is ransacked by the scientific for the comfort and happiness of man. Science has indeed made giant strides during the past centnry, and among the—by no means lest Important—discoveries in medicine comes that of</p>
        <p>THERAPION. This preparation is unquestionably ona of the most; gen- uine and relialele Patent Medicines ever introduced, and ties we understand, been used In the Continental Hospitals by Hicord, 'foetal], aobert. Velpean, Hai.onneuve, the well- known Chaesalgnac. and indeed by all who are regarded as authorities in such matters, mending the celebrated Lalle- mand, and Roux, by whom it was some time linen uniformly adopted, and that it is worthy the attention of those who require such a remedy we think there Is no doubt. From the time of Aristotle downwards a potent agent in the removal of these diseases has, like the famed philosopher's stone been the object of search of some hopeful generous minds ; and for beyond the mere power—lf such could ever have been disc wered—of transmuting the ba4er metal into gold Is surely the diecovery of a remedy so potent as to replenish the falling energies in the one case, and in the other so effectually, speedily and safely to expel from the system the poisons of acquired or Inherited disease in all their protean forms as to leave no taint or trace behind, Such is the new French Remedy TIMAPION, which may certainly rank with, If not take precedence of. many of the discoveries of our day, about which no little Bstentation and noise have been maade. and the extensive and ever-Increas- ing demand that has been created for this medicine wherever Introduced appears to prove that it is destined to cast into oblivion all those questionable remedies that were formerly the sole reliance of medical men. Therapion may be obtained of the principal cbemists and merchants throughout the world.—" Diamond Fields Advortiser.—Kimberley.—For par- ticulars of Therapion, send stamped, addressed envelope to MR. R. JOHNSON,.43 HOLFORD So., LONDON, w.O.</p>
      </div>
