        <p>1 Buckley-street P.S.A. Society. I An open meeting of the above society which was held on Sunday was well-attended, Mr. W. Shaw,presi- dont of the society, occupied the chair and welcomed a large number of new members who had joined that afternoon. Mr. W. Harding,of Farnworth, was the speaker and took for his subject " Look thou upon me and be merciful unto me." Miss Miller (soprano) ably sang a solo, and Mr. A. Bates played two violin solos with pleasing effect. Mies M. Plinston and Mr. A. Trow were the accompanists. Mr. B. Dimelow an Mr. H. Woolley also took part in the service.</p>
