        <p>MEDICAL OPINION On Seaweed, AS A MEDICINE FOR THE STOMACH, LIVER, KIDNEYS, AND BLOOD.</p>
        <p>Dr. KIRILLOFF in a paper communicated to the tastern Siberian Medical Associatioe dealt with the Virtues of Seaweed in blood diseases. He said :—Sea- Weed is widely used as a food in Japan, and as it contains combined lodine, blood diseases, which assume such alarming characteristics in other countries run a com- paratively mild course in Japan. Other medical authorities have from time to time called attention to the remark- able curative and strengthening power of Seaweed, but it remains for Mr. Veno to bring it more forcibly before the notice of the public. VEND'S SEAWEED TONIC is regarded as the stand- preparation of Seaweed, and for that reason is Prescribed by doctors and used in many hospitals. It contains a deep-water species obtained in the Pacific Ocean, and possesses a wonderful strengthening, healing and purifying power, especially applicable to young and old 111 spring and autumn. Its most brilliant effect is produced in stomach, liver, kidney, and blood diseases The extraordinary cures it accomplishes even in the Worst casee is undeniable proof of its superior value as a general strengthening and curative medicine. It 11/Irifles the blood, cures indigestion, wind on the stomach, Iver complaints kidney troubles, female weakness, weak 813(1 painful back, headaches, and is very effective in " HABITUAL CON STI PATIO N." The. proprietors, knowing the great value of this !!edicine, are prepared to guarantee a cure or refund ,‘fle money. This is a very strong stand to take, but it Is quite justified by the great success of the, remedy. Asit for VENO'S SEAWEED TONIC. Price is. and 2s. Pd. per bottle at Chemists and Drug Stores.</p>
