      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1905-03-11_WidnesExaminer_art0163" n="art0163">
        <head>WORICAOrSE</head>
        <p>THE WORICAOrSE</p>
        <p>Mr. Spruce moved that in accordance with a recom- mendation of the visiting committee a new boiler he purchased for the workhouse. Mr. Morris seconded. Mr. Woodward thought the proposal involved the big question of water supply, and he would like to know whether the visiting committee had considered that side of the question. They would have to consider whether it would be more economical to continue with the present water supply or to have the Vwyrny supply. Mr. Morris said the comtnittee had not dealt with the , side of the question they had merely dealt with the question os the provision and a boiler. Mr. Spruce pointed'out that the committee had b een advised by the engineer that whether they continued with the present water supply or chose the Vwyrny supply the new boiler would be necessary. The proposal was carried, and the tender of Messrs Timmins and Son for the erection of the new boiler at a cost of £155 was accepted, on the understanding that the acceptance should cover all costs for the preparation of specifications &amp;c.</p>
      </div>
