        <p>'P RUDENTIAL ASSURANCE COMPANY, LIMITED. ESSI Calm, Cxxxx HOLBORN BARS, LONDON. Summary of the report presented at the FiftY-sixth Annual Meeting, held on 2nd March, 1905. ORDINARY BRANCH.—The numeer of Poilcies is sued during the year was 71,274, assuring the sum of £6,954,650. and producing a New Annual Premium Income of £377,587. The Premiums received during the year were £3,959 ,016. being an increase of £154,160 over the year 973. The Claims of the year amounted to £1,654,753. The number of Death. was 7 139, and 6,259 Endowment Assur- ances matured. The number of Policies in force at the end of the year was 742,147. INDUSTRIAL BRANCH.—The Premiums received during the year were £5,979,335, being an increase of £132.781. The Claims of the year amounted to £2,230,180. The number of Deaths was 233,015, and 3,066 Endowment Assurances matured. The number of Free Policies granted during the year to those Policy-holders of five years' standing who desired to discontinue their payments was 112,606. the number in force being 1,003,377 The number of Fre, Policiei which became Claims daring the year WA! 22,211. The total number of Policies in r,,e at the end of the year was 15,577,161 ; their overage duration is ten and three- quarter years. The Assets of the Company, in both branches, as shown in the Balance Seeet, are £55,359,505, being an increase of £4,142.128 over those of 1923. The Staff Provident Fund, which was founded in 1898 for the beueit of the outdoor staff. shows a satisfactory increase for the year, the total amount standing to the credit of the Fund being £138,280. GENERAL BALANCE SHEET Off THE PRUDENTIAL ASSURANOH COMPANY, LIMITED, BEING THE 81731 MARY OF BOTH BRANCHES, ON Tit 18 31eT DK/EMBER, 1904. LIABILITIES. £ s. d. Shareholders' Capital 1,001,00) 0 0 Reserve Funds! 2.300,007 0 0 Life Assurance Funds ... 51,911.668 7 0 Claims under life policies admitted</p>
